std: current_exe on OpenBSD and EmiBSD, whatever the length of argv

Why a patch: std's current_exe for OpenBSD, which patch 0003 lets EmiBSD
into, reads argv with sysctl(KERN_PROC_ARGS, KERN_PROC_ARGV) and divides
the returned length by a pointer's size with div_exact().unwrap(). That
length covers the pointer array and the strings the kernel stores after
it (OpenBSD's ABI, which EmiBSD's kernel keeps), so it is rarely a
multiple of a pointer's size, and the unwrap panics: cargo, rustc's
driver and any program asking for its path stop. This sizes the buffer by
rounding up, takes as many pointers as the length holds, and keeps them up
to the null one that ends the array; only argv[0] is read, as before. The
same code panics on OpenBSD: offered upstream. Found by the kernel
repository running cargo on EmiBSD (2026-11-11). Written by EmiBSD (ISC)
over upstream's text (Apache-2.0 OR MIT), carried by DevTools over the
pinned tag. Author: Emilio Navarrete Lineros, 2026-11-11.

--- a/library/std/src/sys/paths/unix.rs
+++ b/library/std/src/sys/paths/unix.rs
@@ -240,13 +240,18 @@
         cvt(libc::sysctl(mib, 4, ptr::null_mut(), &mut argv_size, ptr::null_mut(), 0))?;
 
         // ... allocate a buffer for it ...
-        let argc = argv_size.div_exact(size_of::<*const libc::c_char>()).unwrap();
+        let argc = argv_size.div_ceil(size_of::<*const libc::c_char>());
         let mut argv = Vec::<*const libc::c_char>::with_capacity(argc);
 
-        // ... and retrieve the argument array.
+        // ... and retrieve the argument array. The length the kernel returns covers the pointers
+        // and the strings stored after them, so it need not be a multiple of a pointer's size;
+        // only the pointers are read, up to the null one that ends them.
         cvt(libc::sysctl(mib, 4, argv.as_mut_ptr() as *mut _, &mut argv_size, ptr::null_mut(), 0))?;
-        let argc = argv_size.div_exact(size_of::<*const libc::c_char>()).unwrap();
+        let argc = argv_size / size_of::<*const libc::c_char>();
         argv.set_len(argc);
+        if let Some(end) = argv.iter().position(|p| p.is_null()) {
+            argv.truncate(end + 1);
+        }
 
         if argv[0].is_null() {
             return Err(io::const_error!(io::ErrorKind::Uncategorized, "no current exe available"));
